<ContentPage title="Why an Ark?" subtitle="The case for building resilient communities now.">
  <p>
    This page exists because we believe honest assessment of risks is a prerequisite for meaningful action.
    We're not doomsayers. We're builders who take the evidence seriously.
  </p>

  <h2>The Convergence of Risks</h2>
  <p>
    The coming decades face an unprecedented convergence of stressors: geopolitical fragmentation, ecological degradation,
    AI-driven economic disruption, supply chain fragility, and erosion of institutional trust. Any one of these is manageable.
    Together, they create a landscape where systemic shocks become more likely and more severe.
  </p>

  <h2>Scenario Spectrum</h2>
  <p>We plan for a range of futures, not a single prediction:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mild turbulence</strong> — Economic recessions, regional conflicts, supply disruptions. BARK functions as an innovative community and business hub.</li>
    <li><strong>Significant disruption</strong> — Prolonged instability, currency crises, infrastructure failures. BARK's semi-autonomous systems provide resilience while maintaining quality of life.</li>
    <li><strong>Severe systemic stress</strong> — Widespread institutional breakdown. BARK preserves critical knowledge, technology, and humanistic values as a seed for recovery.</li>
    <li><strong>Optimistic trajectory</strong> — The world stabilizes and thrives. BARK becomes a model for sustainable, technology-integrated communities. Nothing is wasted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We're Preserving</h2>
  <p>
    BARK isn't about survival for its own sake. It's about preserving what makes civilization worth having:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Humanistic values</strong> — dignity, cooperation, intellectual freedom, diversity of thought</li>
    <li><strong>Human diversity</strong> — cultural, linguistic, genetic, intellectual diversity as a species-level asset</li>
    <li><strong>Appropriate technology</strong> — the subset of modern technology that a semi-autonomous community can sustain: solar, basic manufacturing, communications, medical, agricultural tech</li>
    <li><strong>Knowledge</strong> — scientific method, engineering practices, medical knowledge, agricultural wisdom — preserved in usable form, not just archived</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why Bolivia?</h2>
  <p>
    Bolivia offers a unique combination: geopolitical distance from major conflict zones, abundant natural resources,
    affordable land, favorable climate in the Yungas, established local communities to integrate with, and a legal
    framework that accommodates cooperative and community-based organizations. The Coroico area specifically offers
    altitude-moderated tropical climate, water access, fertile soil, and proximity to La Paz.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Now?</h2>
  <p>
    Building resilience takes years. Infrastructure, agriculture, community bonds, governance systems — none of these
    can be improvised under pressure. The time to build is while conditions allow it. We're not reacting to a crisis.
    We're preparing while preparation is still possible.
  </p>

